"""Item review for every knowledge-test and chapter-check item (pass 8).

Keyed by bank position ("A1.13" = question_bank.A1[13], "Q5.3" = pilot_slice.PILOT_CHECKS[5][3]).
Each entry maps the item to an assessed objective (curriculum_v2.objectives) and gives an instructor
rationale. Where review found a problem, the entry also carries the revision:

* ``wrong``   — replacement distractors (same domain as the stem, so they are plausible)
* ``correct`` — a reworded key (shorter or more precise); the old key text is replaced everywhere
* ``text``    — a reworded stem (removed answer clues, missing questions, ambiguity)

``stem`` is the first words of the ORIGINAL stem, so a test fails loudly if a bank is reordered and an
entry no longer points at the item it was written for. Original wording stays in question_bank.py /
pilot_slice.py and in git history.
"""


def R(stem, obj, why, correct=None, wrong=None, text=None, fix=None):
    return {'stem': stem, 'obj': obj, 'why': why, 'correct': correct, 'wrong': wrong, 'text': text, 'fix': fix}


